.TH README 1 "September 2026" "readme 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
readme \- open the nearest README file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B readme
[\fB-hlv\fR] [\fIfilename\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B readme
looks for files named
.B README
or beginning with
.B README.
in the current directory. If none are found, it searches immediate child
directories. Matches are sorted without regard to case.
.PP
Without options, the first match opens with
.BR glow (1)
when available, or with
.BR less (1)
otherwise.
.PP
When supplied,
.I filename
restricts the search to that filename or pattern.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I filename
A README filename or pattern to search for in the current directory and its
immediate child directories.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h
Show the help screen.
.TP
.B -l
List matching README files instead of opening one.
.TP
.B -v
Show the version number.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open the current directory's README.md, or one in an immediate child directory:
.nf
.B readme README.md
.fi
.TP
List all Markdown README files:
.nf
.B readme -l 'README.*'
.fi
